$20M attacking El-Sayed, keeping the race close", "Prediction markets price Democratic chances in the low seventies and most raters call it Lean D or Tossup"], "rationale": "Polls through late September show a consistent but narrow Democratic lead, with higher-quality independent surveys slightly stronger for El-Sayed than Republican-affiliated ones, and markets price Democratic odds around 70-73%. Heavy Republican outside spending keeps the race genuinely competitive, but the balance of polling, ratings and money favors a Democratic edge of a few points.", "watch": "A sustained late Republican advertising barrage or a shift among Arab American, Black, or suburban voters could tighten this into a true tossup in the final weeks.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Gary Peters (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Michigan's Senate seat is open with Gary Peters retiring, and the contest between Democrat Abdul El-Sayed and Republican Mike Rogers sits near the top of the national battleground list. The state's partisan lean is even, and polls through late September show El-Sayed ahead by roughly three points, with independent and university-sponsored surveys a bit stronger for him than Republican-affiliated ones. Ten professional ratings split between Lean Democratic and Toss-up, with none placing the race in Republican territory.\n\nMoney is a story on both sides: El-Sayed has out-raised Rogers in candidate funds, but Republican-aligned groups have poured far more into attacking him than Democratic groups have spent against Rogers. Prediction markets put Democratic chances in the low seventies. Harris and other national figures have campaigned with El-Sayed in the final stretch. The race remains genuinely competitive, but the weight of the evidence points to a narrow Democratic edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.7769, "margin": 3.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.7646, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7534, "margin": 3.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7553, "margin": 3.4}]}